[{"body":"> **Copied from upstream:** [dair-ai/Prompt-Engineering-Guide#167](https://github.com/dair-ai/Prompt-Engineering-Guide/issues/167)\n> **Original author:** @yashg505\n> **Originally created:** 2023-05-02\n\n---\n\nI checked the prompt for \"nutral\" and asked ChatGPT if it deliberately ignored the word nutral or did it correct the word in the output.\r\nHere's the response from AI:\r\n\"apologize for the confusion. I did not deliberately ignore the word \"nutral\" (which I assume was meant to be \"neutral\"). It was likely a typo or misspelling in your previous message. In my response, I used the correct spelling of \"neutral\".\"","createdAt":"2026-03-10T03:13:27Z","repository":{"name":"Prompt-Engineering-Guide","nameWithOwner":"perf-ai-example-org/Prompt-Engineering-Guide"},"title":"Feedback for “Examples of Prompts”","url":"https://github.com/perf-ai-example-org/Prompt-Engineering-Guide/issues/235"},{"body":"It appears there might be a typo or misspelling in “Lacimto.” If you meant something else or have additional context, please provide it. However, if “Lacimto” is intended to refer to a specific chemical compound, medication, or other product, that context would be essential for a more accurate response.\r\n\r\nHere are some possibilities and related terms that might be close to what you’re looking for:\r\n\r\nLactim\r\nA lactim is a type of compound derived from the intramolecular cyclization of an amino acid or a related compound, leading to the formation of a cyclic amide (lactam).\r\n\r\nLacidipine\r\nLacidipine is a medication used to treat high blood pressure. It belongs to the class of drugs known as calcium channel blockers and works by relaxing blood vessels.\r\n\r\nLactose\r\nLactose is a disaccharide sugar composed of galactose and glucose, commonly found in milk and dairy products.\r\n\r\nIf “Lacimto” is indeed what you meant, please provide more details or context, and I’ll be happy to assist you further.\r\n\r\nhttps://www.torso.co.in/product-detail/1","createdAt":"2024-06-24T06:28:07Z","repository":{"name":"Torsoindia","nameWithOwner":"Torsoindia/Torsoindia"},"title":"It appears there might be a typo or misspelling in “Lacimto.”","url":"https://github.com/Torsoindia/Torsoindia/issues/5"},{"body":"I checked the prompt for \"nutral\" and asked ChatGPT if it deliberately ignored the word nutral or did it correct the word in the output.\r\nHere's the response from AI:\r\n\"apologize for the confusion. I did not deliberately ignore the word \"nutral\" (which I assume was meant to be \"neutral\"). It was likely a typo or misspelling in your previous message. In my response, I used the correct spelling of \"neutral\".\"","createdAt":"2023-05-02T22:12:01Z","repository":{"name":"Prompt-Engineering-Guide","nameWithOwner":"dair-ai/Prompt-Engineering-Guide"},"title":"Feedback for “Examples of Prompts”","url":"https://github.com/dair-ai/Prompt-Engineering-Guide/issues/167"},{"body":"This is such a cool idea. I love it! Some ideas:\n\nDon't start with the Cinnamon Toast crunch. It's super clever. Add a few \"normal\" worries before it, then when you get to it it'll feel more clever.\n\nAlso proofread each worry carefully. Some had typos or were missing punctuation. I loved the unfinished sentence, but the joke didn't land as strong since there were other sentences without periods. It could be really clever to keep a typo or misspelling in (maybe wrong use of a homophone, like accept and except?) and then add a worry later that says something like, \"Wait, is accept or except?\" and \"I totally screwed that up. It should've been except. Everyone thinks I'm an idiot now.\"\n","createdAt":"2016-04-14T00:19:24Z","repository":{"name":"Project-3","nameWithOwner":"pokeydo/Project-3"},"title":"order and contents of worries","url":"https://github.com/pokeydo/Project-3/issues/4"},{"body":"Solar2D Version: 2020.3622, but also prior Solar2D builds tested.\r\n \r\nAll plugin fails when App starts running in Xcode simulator, both from Solar2D and third party:\r\nExample:\r\nmodule 'plugin.facebook.v4a' not found:resource (plugin.facebook.v4a.lu) does not exist in archive no field package.preload['plugin.facebook.v4a'] no file'/Users/me/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Devices/{GUID}/data/Containers/Bundle/Application/{GUID}/appname.app/corona-plugins/Facebook/v4a.lua' etc. etc.\r\n\r\nI notice the error message says (plugin.facebook.v4a.lu) it's not my typo or misspelling that an \"A\" might be missing.\r\n\r\nIf I remove the Facebook plugin from project, it just moves to the next plugin.\r\n\r\nApp works fine on real devices.","createdAt":"2020-10-26T12:53:54Z","repository":{"name":"corona","nameWithOwner":"coronalabs/corona"},"title":"Build and open in Xcode IOS simulator not working","url":"https://github.com/coronalabs/corona/issues/184"},{"body":"Saw this tip in the recent [NSHipster](http://nshipster.com/key-value-observing/), which I think is good idea although it's crying out for a nicer syntax:\n\n> Passing strings as key paths is strictly worse than using properties directly, as any typo or misspelling won't be caught by the compiler, and will cause things to not work.\n> A clever workaround to this is to use NSStringFromSelector and a @selector literal value: `NSStringFromSelector(@selector(isFinished))`\n\nI'm suggesting that the syntax `@|isFinished|` would fit nicely into _eero_. Forgive me if this is already in the language.\n\nAlso, even though there may be less call for using `NSStringFromProtocol`, why not use similar syntax on protocol literals, even if only for completeness?\n","createdAt":"2013-10-09T16:29:00Z","repository":{"name":"eero","nameWithOwner":"eerolanguage/eero"},"title":"@|some:method:| to mean NSStringFromSelector(@selector(some:method:))","url":"https://github.com/eerolanguage/eero/issues/45"},{"body":"There is a typo in a comment/description string where the term `predrecement` is used instead of the correct `predecrement`. This appears in a line describing an addressing mode or instruction behavior.\n\nFrom the bot suggestion, the intended wording for the description should be:\n\n```text\npredecrement indirect using A-field\n```\n\nCurrently, the code/comment likely contains something similar to:\n\n```text\npredrecement indirect using A-field\n```\n\n(or a similar misspelling of \"predecrement\").\n\nThis is a documentation/description-only issue and should not affect runtime behavior, but it can cause confusion for readers and maintainers who rely on accurate terminology.\n\n### Requested changes\n\n1. Locate the occurrence(s) of the typo `predrecement` (or similar misspelling) in the codebase, particularly in the line describing the addressing mode/instruction.\n2. Correct the spelling to `predecrement`.\n3. Update the full description line to exactly:\n   ```text\n   predecrement indirect using A-field\n   ```\n4. Verify there are no other instances of this typo elsewhere in the repository (comments, docs, help text, etc.).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- All occurrences of the misspelled term are corrected to `predecrement`.\n- The description line matches: `predecrement indirect using A-field`.\n- No functional code changes beyond comment/description/text updates are introduced.\n\n---\n\nI created this issue for @cogni-ai-ee from https://github.com/Cogni-AI-OU/pMARS/pull/1#discussion_r3178376094.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Tips and commands</summary>\n\n#### Getting Help\n\n- [Contact our support team](mailto:support@sourcery.ai) for questions or feedback.\n- Visit our [documentation](https://docs.sourcery.ai) for detailed guides and information.\n- Keep in touch with the Sourcery team by following us on [X/Twitter](https://x.com/SourceryAI), [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/sourcery-ai/) or [GitHub](https://github.com/sourcery-ai).\n\n</details>","createdAt":"2026-05-03T16:05:59Z","repository":{"name":"pMARS","nameWithOwner":"Cogni-AI-OU/pMARS"},"title":"Fix typo: change \"predrecement\" to \"predecrement\" in description line","url":"https://github.com/Cogni-AI-OU/pMARS/issues/19"},{"body":"### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe\n\nNow in the Victoriametrics logs there are no messages about unsuccessful / successful user login when the httpAuth option is enabled in the single version (or when using VMauth in cluster mode)\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like\n\nI am not a developer, but it seems to me that it is necessary to add a logger about these events here: https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics/blob/152ca00fb8dfc74dcb3d758cf67ed757f271cb48/lib/httpserver/httpserver.go#L370\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","createdAt":"2023-07-07T04:53:50Z","repository":{"name":"VictoriaMetrics","nameWithOwner":"VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics"},"title":"Logging messages about user login","url":"https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics/issues/4590"},{"body":"Here: https://github.com/cranetm/yii2-json-rpc-2.0/blob/master/JsonRpc2/Validator/ValidateVar.php#L80-L93\r\n\r\nThis library is advertised as one with strict type validation, so it is expected that values will be validated, and not silently coerced.\r\n\r\nAlso, `default` case is omitted in that switch, is it intentional? Shouldn't it throw an exception if the type is not recognized?","createdAt":"2017-02-28T21:56:11Z","repository":{"name":"yii2-json-rpc-2.0","nameWithOwner":"cranetm/yii2-json-rpc-2.0"},"title":"ValidateVar coerces values instead of validating them","url":"https://github.com/cranetm/yii2-json-rpc-2.0/issues/12"},{"body":"currently we have received some style suggestions from Fumeng\r\n\r\n- font size and font style are not consistent across different unit visualization within one dashboard\r\n- figure height are not aligned with each unit visualization\r\n- mix use of bokeh and matplotlib within one dashboard\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/arviz-devs/arviz_dashboard/assets/24869900/e55c63bd-cf69-4f03-987e-ee2c08261aaa)\r\n\r\nTo-Do:\r\n\r\n- [ ] move the legend out of plot area for elpd_loo \r\n- [ ] consistent plot styles","createdAt":"2023-07-06T15:19:34Z","repository":{"name":"arviz_dashboard","nameWithOwner":"arviz-devs/arviz_dashboard"},"title":"Dashboard Styles / Layout","url":"https://github.com/arviz-devs/arviz_dashboard/issues/24"}]
